# `curl` and `wget` (TASK-27 9a; `make test-apps`, which turns @PORT@ and the
# @TLS...@ ports into numbers). C programs on OpenSSL, zlib and libposix's
# sockets and getrandom, run through the broker from the disk's /bin. The
# disk's /system/tls/roots is the test PKI's root (the production image's
# refusal of it is test-hand-run's); the names come from net.hosts. The
# shell gives each program a connection that reaches the host and port of the
# URL on its line, /system/tls to read, and nothing else.
! panicked
! first process ended
< Type help to begin, or help tour.
< \r\n~>
# The lease takes a few hundred milliseconds under TCG.
> sleep 3\r
< \r\n~>
# HTTP: a page, byte for byte; to a file; under the URL's name.
