# OpenSSL with threads (ADR-0309 item 4): four threads handshake at once over
# one context. Against the valid server every handshake succeeds and returns the
# page; against the expired and the wrong-name servers all are refused (the
# Makefile checks that the servers saw no request byte).
> tlsthreads https://test.zoraya:@TLSVALID@/\r
< 12 handshakes from 4 threads, all verified and served
< \r\n~>
> status\r
< \r\nsucceeded (exit status 0)
< \r\n~>
> tlsthreads -r expired https://expired.zoraya:@TLSEXPIRED@/\r
< 12 handshakes from 4 threads, all refused
< \r\n~>
> status\r
< \r\nsucceeded (exit status 0)
< \r\n~>
> tlsthreads -r name https://wrong.zoraya:@TLSWRONG@/\r
< 12 handshakes from 4 threads, all refused
< \r\n~>
> status\r
< \r\nsucceeded (exit status 0)
< \r\n~>
# The crypto half of ADR-0309 item 4: eight threads of SHA-256, AES-GCM and
# RAND_bytes against a single-threaded reference; a fork child gets no random bytes.
> cryptothreads\r
< 8 threads x 200 rounds of SHA-256, AES-256-GCM and RAND_bytes as the single-threaded; a fork child gets no random bytes
< \r\n~>
> status\r
< \r\nsucceeded (exit status 0)
< \r\n~>
