# Nothing in the programs turns the checks off or changes the roots (ADR-0321,
# INV-0321-1; ADR-0228 item 3, INV-0312-1). The lines below do not match a
# description, so they run with default settings, and the +net word gives the
# network that a transfer would need: the programs themselves refuse each
# option, exit with status 2, and the Makefile checks that the expired and
# wrong-name servers saw 0 request bytes. The roots a --cacert or --capath
# names are readable (+r), the other root of the test PKI.
> +net expired.zoraya:@TLSEXPIRED@ curl -k https://expired.zoraya:@TLSEXPIRED@/\r
